  "body": "The behavior of ctx.fillText(text, x, y, null), ctx.fillText(text, x, y, undefined), ctx.fillText(text, x, y, NaN) is different for different browsers.\n\nFor example:\nChrome: fillText(text, x, y, null) == fillText(text, x, y, NaN) == fillText(text, x, y, 0), while fillText(text, x, y, undefined) == fillText(text, x, y)\n\nEdge: fillText(text, x, y, null) == fillText(text, x, y, undefined) == fillText(text, x, y, NaN) == fillText(text, x, y, 0)\n\nFirefox: fillText(text, x, y, null) == fillText(text, x, y, undefined) == fillText(text, x, y), while fillText(text, x, y, NaN) == fillText(text, x, y, 0)\n\nThe spec should be more clear so that the behavior can be consistent.\n",
